  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best config (config_019: pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.639 acc. All multimodal results so far use pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder; the RNA encoder axis is completely untested. RNA dominates image performance (0.485 vs ~0.21–0.23 image-only), so the quality of the RNA representation likely has the largest leverage on final multimodal accuracy. Question: Does a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) provide a meaningfully better representation than linear PCA, when fused with the known-best image/aggregation/fusion settings? Why this is the best next experiment: It isolates the single largest untested design axis (RNA encoder) while holding all other parameters at their empirically validated best values (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted). A positive result would justify further exploration of scgpt; a null result would confirm PCA sufficiency and redirect budget toward the image-encoder axis (e.g., config_025). This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

